```java
static long reconstruct(long raw, int width, long expected) {
    long modulus = width == 4 ? (1L << 32) : (1L << (8*width));
    long best = raw;
    long bestDistance = Math.abs(raw - expected);
    // candidate raw + modulus
    long candidate = raw + modulus;
    long distance = Math.abs(candidate - expected);
    if (distance < bestDistance || (distance == bestDistance && candidate > best)) { best = candidate; bestDistance = distance; }
    // candidate raw - modulus (if >= 0)
    if (raw >= modulus) {
        candidate = raw - modulus;
        distance = Math.abs(candidate - expected);
        if (distance < bestDistance || (distance == bestDistance && candidate > best)) { best = candidate; bestDistance = distance; }
    }
    return best;
}
```
Note: `Math.abs(raw - expected)`: raw ≤ 2^32-1, expected ≤ 2^62 → the difference fits in long ✓ (2^62 < 2^63). But `raw + modulus` ≤ 2^33 → fine. And `candidate - expected` ≥ -(2^62) ✓.

